From 466b59302f5fdb11514cf7e136d15dc4dbad48d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 10:47:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 860/860] feat(v1): support lockstep PP adaptive verification
 and PP sink rejection

Allow enable_adaptive_verification=True under pipeline_parallel_size > 1 when
adaptive_verification_row_cost is pinned, broadcasting per-step draft
confidences and calibration state via PPHandler and consuming them through
mirrored pp_size-deep FIFOs on both non-last and last PP ranks so every stage
computes identical trimmed batch shapes and dead-row cuts. Also allow
VLLM_SINK_REJECTION=1 on PP > 1 (SinkSampler runs strictly on is_last_pp_rank).

Zero behavior change when pipeline_parallel_size == 1.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Unlocks adaptive verification and sink rejection on PP > 1 shapes (verified LRU 5/5 and +14.5%..+16.9% prose-c1, +13.7% prose-c4, +15%..+23.6% code-c8 on live PP=2, TP=2).
Quality: Bit-identical confidence state across PP stages; verified LRU 5/5 with VLLM_SINK_REJECTION=1 on live PP=2, TP=2.
Tests: pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py
Upstream-status: Local PP adaptive verification and sink rejection support.
